WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.232
Actually, we know that the tariff war

00:00:02.232 --> 00:00:04.421
has been going on for nearly a year now

00:00:04.421 --> 00:00:06.643
. One of the main reasons Trump started

00:00:06.643 --> 00:00:08.709
the tariff war was the issue of trade

00:00:08.709 --> 00:00:09.299
deficits.

00:00:09.299 --> 00:00:11.012
>> Now, a year later, have you noticed

00:00:11.012 --> 00:00:12.774
that Taiwan's trade surplus with the

00:00:12.774 --> 00:00:14.160
U.S. has hit a record high?

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:15.918
>> We are worried that, indeed, while we

00:00:15.918 --> 00:00:17.768
have already made sufficient investment

00:00:17.768 --> 00:00:19.249
commitments in the past, we are

00:00:19.249 --> 00:00:21.007
concerned that you might seize on the

00:00:21.007 --> 00:00:22.912
data and continue to make more demands.

00:00:22.912 --> 00:00:24.882
Are the tariff negotiations between the

00:00:24.882 --> 00:00:26.655
Taiwan government and the U.S. side

00:00:26.655 --> 00:00:28.839
still ongoing? What kind of bottom line

00:00:28.839 --> 00:00:31.060
do we have to ensure our position? Some

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:32.687
countries might think this way: "He

00:00:32.687 --> 00:00:34.358
only has two years left in his term,

00:00:34.358 --> 00:00:35.939
maybe the midterm elections or the

00:00:35.939 --> 00:00:37.701
presidential race will change things,"

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:39.418
so we can just drag it out, and maybe

00:00:39.418 --> 00:00:41.190
after two years, nothing will happen.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.844
How should we view the negotiation

00:00:42.844 --> 00:00:44.735
approach that best serves the interests

00:00:44.735 --> 00:00:46.017
of the Taiwan government?

00:00:46.017 --> 00:00:48.348
>> Yes, well, thank you, Ting-hao, for

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:51.689
bringing this up. It is very important.

00:00:51.689 --> 00:00:54.321
Our tariff negotiations with the U.S.

00:00:54.321 --> 00:00:56.746
are indeed driven by the fact that

00:00:56.746 --> 00:00:59.517
Taiwan's trade surplus with the U.S. is

00:00:59.517 --> 00:01:02.569
too large. There is already an estimate

00:01:02.569 --> 00:01:04.949
for this year that Taiwan's total

00:01:04.949 --> 00:01:07.749
export value will be around 900 billion

00:01:07.749 --> 00:01:09.799
U.S. dollars.

00:01:09.799 --> 00:01:11.984
>> The largest destination for these

00:01:11.984 --> 00:01:14.555
exports is likely the United States, so

00:01:14.555 --> 00:01:17.062
it can be expected that Taiwan's trade

00:01:17.062 --> 00:01:20.282
surplus with the U.S. this year. Will

00:01:20.282 --> 00:01:22.825
be even higher than when he proposed

00:01:22.825 --> 00:01:26.279
reciprocal tariffs last year.

00:01:26.279 --> 00:01:28.955
>> However, we uphold the stance of mutual

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:31.363
benefit; we do not speculate on how

00:01:31.363 --> 00:01:33.973
much time he has left in his term, nor

00:01:33.973 --> 00:01:36.649
do we think we can just drag it out and

00:01:36.649 --> 00:01:40.339
be done with it.

00:01:40.339 --> 00:01:42.375
>> I believe that while these U.S.

00:01:42.375 --> 00:01:44.667
reciprocal tariffs certainly pose a

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:47.150
challenge for Taiwan, they are also an

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:49.314
opportunity for Taiwan to further

00:01:49.314 --> 00:01:51.542
integrate with the U.S. industrial

00:01:51.542 --> 00:01:53.356
structure. Hmm.

00:01:53.356 --> 00:01:55.348
>> This is the mindset we hold.

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:56.530
>> Many people think this might be a

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:57.886
crisis, but you believe it is actually

00:01:57.886 --> 00:01:58.508
an opportunity.

00:01:58.508 --> 00:02:00.186
>> I think this is an opportunity.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.816
>> Because you have to see the development

00:02:01.816 --> 00:02:03.364
of Taiwan's industry; in the past, we

00:02:03.364 --> 00:02:03.913
moved West.

00:02:03.913 --> 00:02:04.882
>> Hmm.

00:02:04.882 --> 00:02:07.701
>> Then we moved South. Later, we moved

00:02:07.701 --> 00:02:09.834
North, cooperating with Japan, and now

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:11.967
we should move East across the Pacific

00:02:11.967 --> 00:02:13.216
to join with the U.S.

00:02:13.216 --> 00:02:14.998
>> It is time for further integration; in

00:02:14.998 --> 00:02:16.735
the history of our industry, the time

00:02:16.735 --> 00:02:18.573
to head in this direction has arrived.

00:02:18.573 --> 00:02:20.222
>> It just so happens that this provided

00:02:20.222 --> 00:02:21.828
an opportunity, and our negotiations

00:02:21.828 --> 00:02:23.521
this time have truly upheld a position

00:02:23.521 --> 00:02:24.403
of mutual benefit.

00:02:24.403 --> 00:02:25.366
>> Hmm.

00:02:25.366 --> 00:02:27.527
>> Meaning we invest in the U.S. And they

00:02:27.527 --> 00:02:29.568
will also come to Taiwan to invest.

00:02:29.568 --> 00:02:31.248
>> That is, Taiwan has a "national team"

00:02:31.248 --> 00:02:33.016
investing in the U.S., and the U.S. has

00:02:33.016 --> 00:02:34.797
a "national team" investing in Taiwan.

00:02:34.797 --> 00:02:36.770
This is true for the tech industry, the

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:38.496
defense industry, as well as other

00:02:38.496 --> 00:02:38.991
sectors.

00:02:38.991 --> 00:02:41.384
>> So, under these conditions of mutual

00:02:41.384 --> 00:02:43.778
benefit, the U.S. also sees Taiwan's

00:02:43.778 --> 00:02:46.120
strength. And sees the necessity of

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.646
Taiwan's industry to U.S. development.

00:02:48.646 --> 00:02:50.579
>> And its importance.

00:02:50.579 --> 00:02:53.112
>> It also shows that the various policies

00:02:53.112 --> 00:02:55.519
proposed by the Taiwan government are

00:02:55.519 --> 00:02:59.519
solid.
